# Working material from runs — see .local/README.md. Never committed.
# UNANCHORED, so a .local/ at any depth is ignored and not only the one at the root. It was
# `/.local/` until 2026-09-16, and a tool writing to `harness/.local/` while that
# directory was the working directory left an untracked file the root rule did not cover.
.local/

# A PROJECT'S KEYS AND A MACHINE'S OWN PINS, never committed (plan 7.0, items 8.6c and 8.2b): the keys
# are the `.env` in the folder above the clone (`KIT/.env` for the KIT's own development), outside this
# repository; these lines are the belt - the gates check the whole tree and a commit is `git add -A` of
# it, so a `.env` placed here by mistake is ignored anywhere in the clone.
# The .env record beside it (item 8.6d) - names and sha256s, never a value - the clone's own.
.env
.env-record.edn
.env.local
.mise.local.toml
